al funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aThe Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) digital-Visual Chart series is designed to meet the needs of users who require georeferenced raster images of FAA Visual Flight Rules (VFR) charts. An Aeronautical Raster Chart is a digital image of an FAA VFR Chart. All information that is part of the paper chart is included in the file. The area inside the neat line is georeferenced to the surface of the earth. Only the main body of the chart is accurately georeferenced. Each digital-Visual Chart is provided in one TIF file. The files are 300 dots per inch and 8-bit color. The product is provided as a GeoTIFF and is available for public viewing from this website. As each paper chart is updated, its raster equivalent is also updated and available for viewing on this website. Please ensure you are using the most current chart by referring to the chart legend. Charts in compressed (ZIP) format contain a TIF, geospatial and metadata files. Additional format charts are provided as Portable Document Format (PDF).  aMerger of: Digital - visual charts (d-VC). Alaska (DVD-ROM); Digital - visual charts (d-VC). East (DVD-ROM); and Digital - visual charts (d-VC). West (DVD-ROM).0 aPage last modified: March 23, 2026 ; title from web page (viewed Mar. 30, 2026). 0aAeronautical chartszUnited States. 0aAeronautical chartszCanada, Eastern. 0aUnited StatesvMaps.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140377 0aCanada, EasternvMaps. 7aAeronautical charts.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026034 7aDigital maps.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026199 7aRaster data.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102652004aUnited States. Federal Aviation Administration. National Aeronautical Navigation Services.tDigital - visual charts (d-VC). Alaskaw(DLC) 20105865